  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Untwist result (2026-10-10)\n\n**Execution note.** The VS Code notebook controller did not execute cells for this notebook in the agent session (runCell: NOT executed), so no cell carries a saved output. Every cell was executed in the shared kernel by loading its source from the saved .wb file (ToExpression of the cell value, in order 3, 4, ..., 24); all numbers below are from those runs. P_HW is the projector orthogonal for the invariant metric G (diag G = 1,1,1,2,6,9,4,9 in the plain GT basis; JJ itself is not Hermitian), which is the EH-frame orthogonal projector. Precision pr = 200 throughout; Baxter residuals are evaluated in exact arithmetic on the stored numbers (the naive norm printed an exact 0 with Precision Infinity, the trap of Clean-CG-combinations 7).\n\n**Section 0.** gl(3) relations, nilpotency, G invariant and positive: True. Quantum determinant deviation 1e-199, [t1,t2] = 1e-197. Factorized x0 = Inverse-based x0 exactly. 21 states (sector sizes 1,2,2,6,10), 6 HW-limit branches (multiplicities 1,1,1,2,1); at eps = 1e-6 the branch raising residual rr is below 4e-7 versus at least 1.3 for the other states; top branch = e1 x e1 to 1e-191; P_HW fractions 1.000; exact Baxter residual of the 21 dual Q's 8.4e-149; vacuum Q's 7e-190 (degrees 0,2,4). Timings: 21 states at one eps 1.5 s; one parameter point 0.02 s.\n\n**Task 0 (exact, symbolic eps, phi = (1/3,-2/7,5/11), om = (3/4,-1/5)).** (i) a' is eps-free and equals the closed form (a'0 = -2275/783). (ii) b'/(a'c') = 1 + eps (24/1225) + O(eps^2), predicted 24/1225. (iii) phi0 = e1^T exp(a'0 E12) exp(c'0 E23) exactly (reversed order is False), b'0 = a'0 c'0, c'0 = 2755/3549. (iv) leading orders of phi/delta^Lambda: (2,1,0),(1,2,0),(2,0,1),(1,0,2),(1,1,1): eps^0; (0,2,1),(0,1,2): eps^1. (0,1,2) eps^1 coefficient = -72/1225 (a'0 c'0)^2 = -3 (t-2)(phi2-om2)(a'0 c'0)^2. Grid 3x6 (identical tables for phi and phi'): ranks (eps^0, eps^1, both) = (1,1,1) dim 2: (1,2,2); (2,1,0): (1,0,1); (1,2,0): (1,0,1); (2,0,1): (1,1,1); (1,0,2): (1,1,1); (0,2,1),(0,1,2): (0,1,1) with all leading orders 1.\n\n**Task 1.** eps-exponents (eps = 1e-6, 2e-6, 4e-6; identical for all 18 om): S / K / ||Psi|| = [4,2,0]: -5 / K = 0 exactly / -2; [4,1,1]: -6 / -5 / -3; [3,3,0]: -6 / -5 / -3; [3,2,1] both copies: -7 / -6 / -4; [2,2,2]: -8 / -8 / -6. Exact undo S = s<phi x e1|P_HW Psi>: deviation below 1e-152 (accuracy) at 324 points. max over the grid of |K/S| at (1e-6, 2e-6, 4e-6): [4,1,1] 9.58e-7, 1.92e-6, 3.83e-6; [3,3,0] 9.35e-7, 1.87e-6, 3.74e-6; octet 1 2.75e-6, 5.5e-6, 1.1e-5; octet 2 1.12e-6, 2.25e-6, 4.5e-6 (all linear in eps); singlet 2.58 at every eps and om. kappa - 1 at om A = (3/4,-1/5) / om B = (7/2,-7/4): [4,1,1] 1.1e-7, 2.19e-7, 4.39e-7 / 7.08e-7, 1.42e-6, 2.83e-6; [3,3,0] 8.63e-8, 1.73e-7, 3.45e-7 / 6.84e-7, 1.37e-6, 2.74e-6; octet 1 1.5e-7, 2.99e-7, 5.99e-7 / 1.98e-6, 3.96e-6, 7.92e-6; octet 2 -9.96e-8, -1.99e-7, -3.98e-7 / -8.22e-7, -1.64e-6, -3.29e-6; singlet kappa = 3.58 (constant). Spec expectation confirmed: kappa -> 1 linearly for [4,1,1], [3,3,0], both octets; singlet kappa != 1. Contamination (eps = 1e-6, om A): singlet carried by site-1 weight (1,0,2) at eps^-8 (fraction 1.0), weights (0,1,2),(0,2,1),(1,1,1) at eps^-7 (1e-7 each), (1,2,0),(2,0,1) at eps^-6, (2,1,0) at eps^-5; octet 1 carried by (1,1,1),(1,2,0),(2,0,1) all at eps^-6 (fractions 0.94, 2.31, 0.37, signed) and (2,1,0) at eps^-5 (7e-8). Sum of contributions = K to 1e-16 or better.\n\n**Task 2.** Vacuum Baxter residual max 6.9e-190, dual Q's 8.4e-149. NB the spec's w3 = 1 + eps 2/9 coincides with w2 at om2 = 2/9 (vacuum Q Baxter residual 4e-10); w3 = 1 + eps 5/13 is used (w3 drops out). R_C/R_Q state independence over the 6 branches (max over 18 om): 1.56e-116 (eps = 1e-6), 1.34e-125 (4e-6); over all 21 states: 2.4e-116, 1.0e-126; R_Q keeps 126 digits (limit of the chosen pr, not of the identity). Qnum = R_C to the same numbers. CG extraction (spread of C^Q over the 18 om / error vs chain side) at eps = 1e-6: [4,1,1] 8.5e-7 / 7.9e-7; [3,3,0] 8.5e-7 / 9.4e-7; octet 1 3.5e-6 / 3.4e-6; octet 2 1.6e-6 / 1.8e-6; at 4e-6: 3.4e-6 / 3.2e-6, 3.4e-6 / 3.7e-6, 1.4e-5 / 1.4e-5, 6.3e-6 / 7.3e-6 (scaling 4.00 +- 0.00001 in eps). 27 trivial check: deviation below 1e-144 (accuracy). hat = phi0_(1,1,1)/(a'0 c'0) = (1,3), om-independent. Richardson (second order, eps = 1e-6, 2e-6, 4e-6, om A, f = C eps^-p_B): [4,1,1] 46.67453891 (chain) vs 46.67453891 (Q), agreement 1.2e-19; [3,3,0] 10.92853892, 1.6e-121; octet 1 184.3305612, 3.2e-20; octet 2 -238.5587523, 9.5e-20.\n\n**Task 3.** Q-number identity <v2 x v2|Psi>/<x0|Psi> = det6[Fvac(w1,y)]/psiQ (top-normalized) holds to 1.6e-116. rho_B = K^tk/S (literal spec definition): octets rho_B = O(eps), so the eps-independent quantity is g = rho_B/eps; singlet rho_B is eps-independent. (a) eps-independence of g (1e-6 vs 4e-6, max over 18 om): octet 1 3.0e-6, octet 2 1.7e-6, singlet 6.1e-6 (O(eps)); rho_B(4e-6)/rho_B(1e-6) = 4.000 for the octets. (b) phi-independence: singlet g(phi')/g(phi) = 1 - 3e-8 (independent); octets NOT phi-independent (ratios octet 1: 3.90, 0.729, 1.158, -0.245; octet 2: 2.16, 0.805, 1.103, -0.190 at 4 om). (c) eps -> 0 values g0 = (4g(1e-6) - g(4e-6))/3: singlet g0 = 31/12 for all 18 om (1 distinct value); octets: 6 distinct values over the 18 om = depend on om2 only (om1-only ratios equal 1 to display precision); octet 1 g0 at om2 = (-1/5, 9/7, -12/5, 5/3, 2/9, -7/4): 0.14973237, -1.60554326, 2.74889052, -2.05561394, -0.3490959597, ...; octet 2 at om2 = -1/5: -0.0996172. Rationalized (1e-9) octet values are not simple (e.g. 3217/21485); the 1e-9 tolerance does not make them evidence of exactness. Singlet K/S = 2.5833 independent of eps, om, phi: contamination ratio structural as in Clean-CG.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
