  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Task 5 prerequisites (self-contained: deltaL, idxOf, t3Data are re-stated so the cell does not depend on the state of cells 20, 23). F(eps, om; phi) = Qnum^tk/(delta^Lambda a'0 c'0), Qnum^tk = Qnum - T = R_C - T (Qnum = R_C to 1e-116, Task 2; T = delta^Lambda s <v2(x)v2|Psi>/<x0|Psi> is itself a Q-number, Task 3). *)\ndeltaL[R_] := 1/((R[\"w2\"] - R[\"z\"][[1]])^2 (R[\"w2\"] - R[\"z\"][[2]]));\nidxOf[wt_] := u12idx[[Position[u12wts, wt][[1, 1]]]];\nidx111 = idxOf[{1, 1, 1}];\nvecsAt[R_] := Module[{zz = R[\"z\"], w1 = R[\"w1\"], y = R[\"y\"], v1, v2, ph},\n  v1 = u12v1[zz, w1, y]; v2 = u12v2[zz, w1, y]; ph = u12phi[zz, w1, y];\n  <|\"v12\" -> N[Flatten[KroneckerProduct[v1, v2]], pr], \"phe1\" -> N[v2[[1]] Flatten[KroneckerProduct[ph, u12e1]], pr]|>];\nt3Data[ph_, ie_, om_] := Module[{R = reg[epsL[[ie]], ph, om[[1]], om[[2]]], B, zz, V, v2, v2v2, dl, p1},\n  zz = R[\"z\"]; B = branchesAt[zz]; p1 = t1Point[B, R]; dl = deltaL[R];\n  v2 = u12v2[zz, R[\"w1\"], R[\"y\"]]; v2v2 = N[Flatten[KroneckerProduct[v2, v2]], pr];\n  Table[With[{psi = brOf[B, hwList[[ib, 1]], hwList[[ib, 2]]][\"psi\"], d = p1[[ib]]}, With[{T = dl v2[[1]] (v2v2 . psi)}, <|\"S\" -> d[\"S\"], \"K\" -> d[\"K\"], \"T\" -> T, \"RCtk\" -> d[\"RC\"] - T, \"Ktk\" -> d[\"K\"] - T, \"rho\" -> (d[\"K\"] - T)/d[\"S\"]|>]], {ib, 6}]];\nphis8 = {{1/3, -2/7, 5/11}, {-2/5, 3/8, 7/11}, {1/2, 1/5, -3/7}, {2/3, -1/4, 1/9}, {-1/3, 4/7, 2/5}, {3/5, 1/8, -1/6}, {1/7, -3/5, 2/3}, {5/8, -2/9, 1/4}};\nom5 = Flatten[Table[{o1, o2}, {o1, {3/4, 7/2}}, {o2, om2s}], 1];\nchecks[\"T5 no om component equals a phi component\"] = And @@ Flatten[Table[! MemberQ[ph, o], {ph, phis8}, {o, Union[Flatten[om5]]}]];\na0G[ph_, om_] := (om[[1]] - ph[[1]]) (ph[[2]] - ph[[1]])/((om[[1]] - ph[[2]]) (om[[2]] - ph[[2]]));\nc0G[ph_, om_] := ((om[[1]] - ph[[2]]) (ph[[1]] - ph[[3]])/((ph[[1]] - ph[[2]]) (om[[1]] - ph[[3]]) ) (ph[[3]] - ph[[2]]))/(om[[2]] - ph[[3]]);\nchecks[\"T5 c0G reproduces c'0 = 2755/3549 at phiP, om A\"] = c0G[phiP, {3/4, -1/5}] === 2755/3549;\nepsL5 = {10^-6, 2 10^-6, 4 10^-6};\nvandInv = Inverse[Table[epsL5[[ie]]^j, {ie, 3}, {j, 0, 2}]];\nuV = (u12e1 . Ee[1, 3])[[idx111]]; upV = (u12e1 . Ee[2, 3] . Ee[1, 2])[[idx111]];\nchecks[\"T5 u, u' supported on the (1,1,1) indices; u + u' = (1,3)\"] = {Total[Abs[u12e1 . Ee[1, 3]]] == Total[Abs[uV]], Total[Abs[u12e1 . Ee[2, 3] . Ee[1, 2]]] == Total[Abs[upV]], uV + upV === {1, 3}, uV, upV};\n(* phi_scaled restricted to (1,1,1) = b' u + a'c' u' (exact, eps = 1e-6, phi, om A) *)\nchecks[\"T5 phi_scaled(1,1,1) = b' u + a'c' u' (exact equality at eps = 1e-6)\"] = Module[{R = reg[10^-6, phiP, 3/4, -1/5], dl, n, np},\n   dl = DiagonalMatrix[Table[1/(R[\"w2\"] - R[\"z\"][[k]]), {k, 3}]]; n = u12nMat[R[\"z\"], R[\"w1\"], R[\"y\"]]; np = Inverse[dl] . n . dl . Inverse[n];\n   (u12phi[R[\"z\"], R[\"w1\"], R[\"y\"]]/deltaL[R])[[idx111]] === np[[1, 3]] uV + np[[1, 2]] np[[2, 3]] upV];\nGrid[{{\"checks\", ToString[Normal[checks][[-4 ;; -1, 2]]]}}, Frame -> All]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* f(eps) := F(eps) eps^4 (octet ||Psi|| ~ eps^-4, Task 1) = F0 + eps F1 + eps^2 F2 from eps = 1e-6, 2e-6, 4e-6 (three points, exact 3x3 inverse; two points would leave an O(eps) error in F1); g = F1/F0 fitted by a straight line in om2 (explicit least squares). The signal's own slope is -(t-2) R_c, R_c = (u.C)/((u+u').C), u = e1^T E13, u' = e1^T E23 E12 on the (1,1,1) indices, C = chain-side [P_HW Psi_c]_((1,1,1), e1); Delta_c = slope + (t-2) R_c. *)\nlineFit[xs_, ys_] := Module[{xm = Mean[xs], ym = Mean[ys], sl}, sl = Total[(xs - xm) (ys - ym)]/Total[(xs - xm)^2]; {sl, ym - sl xm, Max[Abs[ys - (ym - sl xm + sl xs)]]}];\nt5Phi[ph_] := Module[{dat, out},\n  dat = Table[Table[t3Data[ph, ie, om], {ie, 3}], {om, om5}];\n  out = Table[Module[{co, F0, g, fa, fb, b, C},\n     co = Table[vandInv . Table[With[{R = reg[epsL5[[ie]], ph, om5[[io, 1]], om5[[io, 2]]]}, epsL5[[ie]]^4 dat[[io, ie, ib, \"RCtk\"]]/(deltaL[R] a0G[ph, om5[[io]]] c0G[ph, om5[[io]]])], {ie, 3}], {io, 12}];\n     F0 = co[[All, 1]]; g = co[[All, 2]]/co[[All, 1]];\n     fa = lineFit[om2s, g[[1 ;; 6]]]; fb = lineFit[om2s, g[[7 ;; 12]]];\n     b = brOf[branchesAt[reg[epsL5[[1]], ph, 1, 1][\"z\"]], {3, 2, 1}, ib - 3];\n     C = PHWc[{3, 2, 1}][b[\"psi\"]][[(idx111 - 1) d1 + 1]];\n     <|\"ib\" -> ib, \"F0spread\" -> Max[Abs[F0/F0[[1]] - 1]], \"slope\" -> fa[[1]], \"icpt\" -> fa[[2]], \"lineRes\" -> fa[[3]], \"dSlope\" -> fb[[1]] - fa[[1]], \"dIcpt\" -> fb[[2]] - fa[[2]], \"lineRes2\" -> fb[[3]], \"F0\" -> F0[[1]], \"R\" -> (uV . C)/((uV + upV) . C)|>], {ib, {4, 5}}];\n  out];\n{tT5a, t5one} = AbsoluteTiming[t5Phi[phiP]];\nGrid[Join[{{\"time one phi (s)\", tT5a}}, Table[{c, ToString[Map[N[Re[#], 8] &, KeyDrop[t5one[[c]], \"ib\"]]]}, {c, 2}]], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* all 8 directions; contamination slope Delta_c(phi) = slope_c + (t-2) R_c *)\n{tT5, t5res} = AbsoluteTiming[Table[t5Phi[ph], {ph, phis8}]];\nrChain2 = Table[With[{b = brOf[branchesAt[reg[epsL5[[2]], ph, 1, 1][\"z\"]], {3, 2, 1}, c]}, With[{C = PHWc[{3, 2, 1}][b[\"psi\"]][[(idx111 - 1) d1 + 1]]}, (uV . C)/((uV + upV) . C)]], {ph, phis8}, {c, 2}];\ndelta5 = Table[Table[Re[t5res[[i, c, \"slope\"]] + (t12 - 2) t5res[[i, c, \"R\"]]], {c, 2}], {i, 8}];\nratios5 = Table[{(ph[[1]] - ph[[2]])/(ph[[2]] - ph[[3]]), (ph[[2]] - ph[[3]])/(ph[[3]] - ph[[1]]), ph[[2]]/(ph[[2]] - ph[[1]])}, {ph, phis8}];\nGrid[Join[{{\"phi\", \"copy\", \"F0\", \"slope\", \"intercept\", \"line resid (om1=3/4)\", \"slope diff om1=7/2\", \"icpt diff\", \"F0 spread\", \"R_c chain (1e-6)\", \"R_c (2e-6)\", \"Delta_c\", \"r1\", \"r2\", \"r3\"}}, Flatten[Table[Table[{phis8[[i]], c, N[Re[t5res[[i, c, \"F0\"]]], 8], N[Re[t5res[[i, c, \"slope\"]]], 10], N[Re[t5res[[i, c, \"icpt\"]]], 10], ScientificForm[N[t5res[[i, c, \"lineRes\"]], 3]], ScientificForm[N[Abs[t5res[[i, c, \"dSlope\"]]], 3]], ScientificForm[N[Abs[t5res[[i, c, \"dIcpt\"]]], 3]], ScientificForm[N[t5res[[i, c, \"F0spread\"]], 3]], N[Re[t5res[[i, c, \"R\"]]], 10], N[Re[rChain2[[i, c]]], 10], N[delta5[[i, c]], 10], N[ratios5[[i, 1]], 6], N[ratios5[[i, 2]], 6], N[ratios5[[i, 3]], 6]}, {c, 2}], {i, 8}], 1], {{\"time (s)\", tT5}}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Follow-up result (Tasks 4-5)\n\n**Task 4.** The singlet contamination ratio is K/S = -t/(3(t-2)), kappa = 1 + K/S = 2(t-3)/(3(t-2)) (kappa(P1) = 43/12; K/S(P1) = 31/12). [The first version of this note reported -(62/105)/(t-2); that came from the HoldAll `DownValues` purge bug of the scan, fixed in cell 36; see Tasks 6-7.] Verified in fresh kernels and with the fixed purge (cell 36): max |K/S + t/(3(t-2))| = 3.1e-11 over t = 29/15, 5/2, 3/2, 7/3, 11/4, 13/5, 9/4, 17/6 (both om), and at P2. Singlet Q-side CG at P1: C^Q = Qnum/(kappa phi012(eps,om)), phi012 the exact (0,1,2) component of u12phi: spread over 18 om / error vs chain side = 1.27e-6 / 1.47e-6 at eps = 1e-6 and 5.06e-6 / 5.89e-6 at 4e-6 (both linear in eps); Richardson limit of C^Q eps^6 (p = -6): chain -5118.53831440474756, Q -5118.53831440474756, agreement 4.5e-19.\n\n**Task 5.** f(eps) = F eps^4 (octet ||Psi|| ~ eps^-4) = F0 + eps F1 + eps^2 F2 from eps = 1e-6, 2e-6, 4e-6; g = F1/F0. F0 is om-independent to 4.8e-17 (max over 8 phi); g is linear in om2 to 2.1e-11 (copy 1) and 9.6e-12 (copy 2) (the residual is O(eps^2)); om1-independence: slope and intercept differences between om1 = 3/4 and 7/2 are exactly 0 (below 1e-168). Slope_c is phi-INDEPENDENT: copy 1 -1.5687193188 (spread over 8 phi 8.4e-12), copy 2 0.7163668808 (2e-12). R_c^chain (eps = 1e-6): copy 1 -1.694366(87..47) (phi-spread 4e-7), copy 2 1.0955643. Contamination slope Delta_c = slope_c + (t-2) R_c with t - 2 = -8/35: Delta_1 in [-1.18143555, -1.18143546], Delta_2 in [0.46595216, 0.46595223], i.e. (b) CONSTANT in phi (spread 9e-8 / 6e-8, O(eps)), nonzero. Intercepts (copy 1 / copy 2) for phi_1..phi_8: -0.61094363/0.23769266; 1.0601633/0.12928700; 0.71772926/0.21339429; -0.43148812/0.32379683; 1.6209228/0.16017655; 0.59069848/0.33146463; -1.5764312/0.084012979; -0.34003978/0.35777099. F0 (copy 1 / 2): phi_1 184.33056 / -238.55875, phi_2 38.959638 / -50.421170, phi_3 120.6600 / -156.1569, phi_4 -37.59970 / 48.66116; F0_2/F0_1 = -1.29418 for each phi shown. The intercept is phi-dependent (this is where the phi-dependence of rho_B sits). Copy labels (ordered by Re eigenvalue) are consistent across phi (same slope per copy). The closed form of Delta_c is in Tasks 6-7 (cell 40).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## Task 6. Leak test of K/S = -(62/105)/(t-2)\n\nProtocol: kernel restarted, then cell 3 evaluated with its line `hN = 1/2; thN = {2/7, -3/5};` replaced by the test point (so no P1 number is ever defined), then cells 4-9 and 14 unchanged, then the cell below. Runs: (h, theta) = (1, (5/2, 0)), (1/3, (1/5, -4/9)), and (1, (7/3, 0)) with phi and phi'.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* K/S of the singlet at the current (hN, thN) of the session: eps = 1e-6, 2e-6, first-order Richardson, om A; optionally another phi *)\nksRichF[ph_, om_] := Module[{f = Table[With[{R = reg[e, ph, om[[1]], om[[2]]]}, With[{d = t1Point[branchesAt[R[\"z\"]], R][[6]]}, d[\"K\"]/d[\"S\"]]], {e, {10^-6, 2 10^-6}}]}, {2 f[[1]] - f[[2]], f}];\nfreshOut = With[{k = ksRichF[phiP, {3/4, -1/5}]}, {hN, thN, t12, y0, -(62/105)/(t12 - 2), Re[k[[1]]]}];\nGrid[{{\"h, theta, t, y0\", ToString[freshOut[[1 ;; 4]]]}, {\"law -(62/105)/(t-2)\", N[freshOut[[5]], 14]}, {\"K/S (Richardson), 14 digits\", N[freshOut[[6]], 14]}, {\"difference\", ScientificForm[N[freshOut[[6]] - freshOut[[5]], 3]]}}, Frame -> All]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* LEAK FOUND. DownValues has attribute HoldAll, so in the Task 4 `purge[]` the line `Do[DownValues[f] = ..., {f, {Tm, ...}}]` assigned to the Do iterator f, not to Tm, tBasisC, tZof, wgt, branchesAt: the memoized transfer matrices and states of the first point (P1) were never purged and the scan kept P1 transfer matrices while y0, th12 changed. Hence K/S = -t12(P1)/(3(t-2)) = -(62/105)/(t-2): the numerator was P1's stale t12. Fixed purge (literal symbols), and the 8-point scan redone; also a check against the fresh-kernel values. *)\nClearAll[purge];\npurge[] := (DownValues[Tm] = Select[DownValues[Tm], ! FreeQ[#[[1]], Pattern] &]; DownValues[tBasisC] = Select[DownValues[tBasisC], ! FreeQ[#[[1]], Pattern] &]; DownValues[tZof] = Select[DownValues[tZof], ! FreeQ[#[[1]], Pattern] &]; DownValues[wgt] = Select[DownValues[wgt], ! FreeQ[#[[1]], Pattern] &]; DownValues[branchesAt] = Select[DownValues[branchesAt], ! FreeQ[#[[1]], Pattern] &];);\nsetPoint[hh_, ths_] := (hN = hh; thN = ths; th12 = thN[[1]] - thN[[2]]; t12 = th12/hN; y0 = (th12 - hN)/(th12 - 2 hN); th1 = thN[[1]]; purge[]);\ntList6 = {29/15, 5/2, 3/2, 7/3, 11/4, 13/5, 9/4, 17/6}; omB6 = {7/2, -7/4};\n{tScan2, scan6} = AbsoluteTiming[Table[setPoint[1, {t, 0}]; {t, Re[ksRichF[phiP, {3/4, -1/5}][[1]]], Re[ksRichF[phiP, omB6][[1]]], -t/(3 (t - 2))}, {t, tList6}]];\nphiScan6 = (setPoint[1, {7/3, 0}]; Re[ksRichF[phiC, {3/4, -1/5}][[1]]]);\nh13scan = (setPoint[1/3, {1/5, -4/9}]; Re[ksRichF[phiP, {3/4, -1/5}][[1]]]);\nsetPoint[1/2, {2/7, -3/5}];\nchecks[\"T6 corrected scan: max |K/S - (-t/(3(t-2)))| over 8 t, om A and om B\"] = N[Max[Abs[Table[{r[[2]] - r[[4]], r[[3]] - r[[4]]}, {r, scan6}]]], 3];\nchecks[\"T6 phi' at t = 7/3 vs -t/(3(t-2)) = -7/3\"] = {N[phiScan6, 14], N[phiScan6 + 7/3, 3]};\nchecks[\"T6 h = 1/3 theta = (1/5,-4/9), t = 29/15 via setPoint\"] = {N[h13scan, 14], N[h13scan - 62/7*0 - (-(29/15)/(3 (29/15 - 2))), 3]};\nGrid[Prepend[Table[{r[[1]], N[r[[2]], 12], N[r[[3]], 12], N[r[[4]], 12], ScientificForm[N[r[[2]] - r[[4]], 3]]}, {r, scan6}], {\"t\", \"K/S (om A)\", \"K/S (om B)\", \"-t/(3(t-2))\", \"A - law\"}], Frame -> All]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Task 7 data. For each (h, theta), phi = phiP, om1 = 3/4 and the six om2, three eps (exact 3x3 Richardson, t5Phi of cell 31): slope_c of g = F1/F0; R_c = (u.C)/((u+u').C) Richardson-extrapolated over the three eps (second order); tau_c = t2-eigenvalue at u = theta1 + h read from the branch's t2 polynomial, Richardson-extrapolated; Delta_c = slope_c + (t-2) R_c. Copies are sorted by tau. *)\nrich[f_] := Module[{r1 = 2 f[[1]] - f[[2]], r2 = 2 f[[2]] - f[[3]]}, {r1, r2, (4 r1 - r2)/3}];\nt7Point[h_, th_] := Module[{res, out},\n  setPoint[h, th]; res = t5Phi[phiP];\n  out = Table[Module[{bs, Rf, tf, sl, R, tau},\n     bs = Table[brOf[branchesAt[reg[epsL5[[ie]], phiP, 1, 1][\"z\"]], {3, 2, 1}, c], {ie, 3}];\n     Rf = Table[With[{C = PHWc[{3, 2, 1}][b[\"psi\"]][[(idx111 - 1) d1 + 1]]}, (uV . C)/((uV + upV) . C)], {b, bs}];\n     tf = Table[b[\"tt\"][[2]] /. u -> th[[1]] + h, {b, bs}];\n     sl = Re[res[[c, \"slope\"]]]; R = Re[rich[Rf][[3]]]; tau = Re[rich[tf][[3]]];\n     <|\"slope\" -> sl, \"R\" -> R, \"tau\" -> tau, \"Delta\" -> sl + ((th[[1]] - th[[2]])/h - 2) R, \"lineRes\" -> res[[c, \"lineRes\"]]|>], {c, 2}];\n  SortBy[out, #[\"tau\"] &]];\ntList7 = {29/15, 5/2, 3/2, 7/3, 11/4, 13/5, 9/4, 17/6, 19/7, 8/3};\n{tT7, t7res} = AbsoluteTiming[Table[{t, t7Point[1, {t, 0}]}, {t, tList7}]];\nt7P1 = t7Point[1/2, {2/7, -3/5}];\nsetPoint[1/2, {2/7, -3/5}];\nGrid[Join[{{\"t\", \"Delta1\", \"Delta2\", \"tau1\", \"tau2\"}}, Table[{r[[1]], N[r[[2, 1, \"Delta\"]], 12], N[r[[2, 2, \"Delta\"]], 12], N[r[[2, 1, \"tau\"]], 12], N[r[[2, 2, \"tau\"]], 12]}, {r, t7res}], {{\"P1\", N[t7P1[[1, \"Delta\"]], 12], N[t7P1[[2, \"Delta\"]], 12], N[t7P1[[1, \"tau\"]], 12], N[t7P1[[2, \"tau\"]], 12]}, {\"time (s)\", tT7, \"\", \"\", \"\"}}], Frame -> All]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* analysis: symmetric combinations, ansatz Delta_c = A + B tau_c, rational fits of degree <= 2/<= 2 on the first 7 t, validation on the last 3 *)\ntl = t7res[[All, 1]];\nD1 = t7res[[All, 2, 1, \"Delta\"]]; D2 = t7res[[All, 2, 2, \"Delta\"]]; T1 = t7res[[All, 2, 1, \"tau\"]]; T2v = t7res[[All, 2, 2, \"tau\"]];\nBv = (D1 - D2)/(T1 - T2v); Av = D1 - Bv T1;\nseries = <|\"Delta1+Delta2\" -> D1 + D2, \"Delta1 Delta2\" -> D1 D2, \"tau1+tau2\" -> T1 + T2v, \"tau1 tau2\" -> T1 T2v, \"A\" -> Av, \"B\" -> Bv|>;\nfitRat[ys_, tr_, te_] := Module[{M, uu, ss, vv, P, Q, ev},\n  M = N[Table[{1, tl[[i]], tl[[i]]^2, -ys[[i]], -ys[[i]] tl[[i]], -ys[[i]] tl[[i]]^2}, {i, tr}], 30];\n  {uu, ss, vv} = SingularValueDecomposition[M]; P = vv[[1 ;; 3, -1]]; Q = vv[[4 ;; 6, -1]];\n  ev[t_] := (P . {1, t, t^2})/(Q . {1, t, t^2});\n  <|\"sv\" -> Diagonal[ss][[-2 ;;]], \"trainRes\" -> Max[Table[Abs[ev[tl[[i]]] - ys[[i]]], {i, tr}]], \"testRes\" -> Table[Abs[ev[tl[[i]]] - ys[[i]]], {i, te}], \"ev\" -> ev, \"P\" -> P/Q[[-1]], \"Q\" -> Q/Q[[-1]]|>];\nfits = Association[Table[k -> fitRat[N[series[k], 25], Range[7], {8, 9, 10}], {k, Keys[series]}]];\nratz = Association[Table[k -> (Rationalize[N[#, 20], 10^-9] & /@ series[k]), {k, Keys[series]}]];\nt1P = 62/35;\np1vals = <|\"Delta1+Delta2\" -> t7P1[[1, \"Delta\"]] + t7P1[[2, \"Delta\"]], \"Delta1 Delta2\" -> t7P1[[1, \"Delta\"]] t7P1[[2, \"Delta\"]], \"tau1+tau2\" -> t7P1[[1, \"tau\"]] + t7P1[[2, \"tau\"]], \"tau1 tau2\" -> t7P1[[1, \"tau\"]] t7P1[[2, \"tau\"]], \"A\" -> t7P1[[1, \"Delta\"]] - (t7P1[[1, \"Delta\"]] - t7P1[[2, \"Delta\"]])/(t7P1[[1, \"tau\"]] - t7P1[[2, \"tau\"]]) t7P1[[1, \"tau\"]], \"B\" -> (t7P1[[1, \"Delta\"]] - t7P1[[2, \"Delta\"]])/(t7P1[[1, \"tau\"]] - t7P1[[2, \"tau\"]])|>;\nGrid[Join[{{\"series\", \"two smallest sv\", \"max train res (7 pts)\", \"test res (3 pts)\", \"P1: value, formula(62/35), diff\"}}, Table[{k, ToString[N[fits[k][\"sv\"], 3]], ScientificForm[N[fits[k][\"trainRes\"], 3]], ToString[N[fits[k][\"testRes\"], 3]], ToString[N[{p1vals[k], fits[k][\"ev\"][t1P], p1vals[k] - fits[k][\"ev\"][t1P]}, 8]]}, {k, Keys[series]}]], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Cell 38 result: Delta1+Delta2 is rational of degree <= 2/2 (held-out 1e-13), the others are not of degree <= 2/2; the tau's carry a scale: t2 has degree 4 in (u, theta, h), so tau/h^4 is the h-independent quantity (P1 has h = 1/2: factor 16). More data (12 further t, h = 1) and a search over degrees (m, n) with m + n <= 10, train on 2/3 of the 22 points, validate on the rest (relative residual); coefficients normalised to leading Q coefficient 1 and rationalized (1e-8). *)\ntList7b = {19/8, 23/9, 31/10, 5/3, 7/4, 12/5, 13/4, 10/3, 17/5, 5/4, 9/5, 26/9};\n{tT7b, t7resB} = AbsoluteTiming[Table[{t, t7Point[1, {t, 0}]}, {t, tList7b}]];\nsetPoint[1/2, {2/7, -3/5}];\nallres = Join[t7res, t7resB]; tlA = allres[[All, 1]];\nD1a = allres[[All, 2, 1, \"Delta\"]]; D2a = allres[[All, 2, 2, \"Delta\"]]; T1a = allres[[All, 2, 1, \"tau\"]]; T2a = allres[[All, 2, 2, \"tau\"]];\nBa = (D1a - D2a)/(T1a - T2a); Aa = D1a - Ba T1a;\nseriesA = <|\"Delta1+Delta2\" -> D1a + D2a, \"Delta1 Delta2\" -> D1a D2a, \"tau1+tau2\" -> T1a + T2a, \"tau1 tau2\" -> T1a T2a, \"A\" -> Aa, \"B\" -> Ba|>;\ntrainIx = Select[Range[22], Mod[#, 3] != 0 &]; testIx = Complement[Range[22], trainIx];\nratFit[ys_, m_, n_] := Module[{M, uu, ss, vv, P, Q, ev, sc = Max[Abs[ys]]},\n  M = N[Table[Join[Table[tlA[[i]]^j, {j, 0, m}], Table[-ys[[i]] tlA[[i]]^j, {j, 1, n}]], {i, trainIx}], 30];\n  {uu, ss, vv} = SingularValueDecomposition[M]; P = vv[[1 ;; m + 1, -1]]; Q = Join[{0}, vv[[m + 2 ;;, -1]]];\n  (* column for -y t^0 is absent: Q0 = 1 by the normalisation y = P/(1 + sum Q_j t^j); the SVD vector gives a least-squares null direction, rescale by its constant-term convention *)\n  {P, vv[[m + 2 ;;, -1]], M}];\nratFit2[ys_, m_, n_] := Module[{M, sol, P, Q, ev, sc = Max[Abs[ys]], resTr, resTe},\n  (* y (1 + q1 t + ... + qn t^n) = p0 + ... + pm t^m, linear least squares for (p, q) *)\n  M = N[Table[Join[Table[tlA[[i]]^j, {j, 0, m}], Table[-ys[[i]] tlA[[i]]^j, {j, 1, n}]], {i, trainIx}], 30];\n  sol = LeastSquares[M, N[ys[[trainIx]], 30]];\n  P = sol[[1 ;; m + 1]]; Q = Prepend[sol[[m + 2 ;;]], 1];\n  ev[t_] := (P . Table[t^j, {j, 0, m}])/(Q . Table[t^j, {j, 0, n}]);\n  resTr = Max[Abs[Table[ev[tlA[[i]]] - ys[[i]], {i, trainIx}]]]/sc; resTe = Max[Abs[Table[ev[tlA[[i]]] - ys[[i]], {i, testIx}]]]/sc;\n  <|\"m\" -> m, \"n\" -> n, \"train\" -> resTr, \"test\" -> resTe, \"P\" -> P, \"Q\" -> Q, \"ev\" -> ev|>];\nsearchFit[ys_] := Module[{found = None},\n  Do[Do[With[{n = s - m}, If[found === None && m + n + 1 <= Length[trainIx] - 2, With[{f = ratFit2[ys, m, n]}, If[f[\"test\"] < 10^-8 && f[\"train\"] < 10^-8, found = f]]]], {m, 0, s}], {s, 0, 10}]; found];\nfitsA = Association[Table[k -> searchFit[N[seriesA[k], 25]], {k, Keys[seriesA]}]];\ncoefTab[f_] := If[f === None, \"no fit with m+n <= 10 (test < 1e-8)\", {f[\"m\"], f[\"n\"], N[f[\"test\"], 3], Rationalize[Chop[N[f[\"P\"], 15], 10^-9], 10^-7], Rationalize[Chop[N[f[\"Q\"], 15], 10^-9], 10^-7]}];\n(* P1 check, tau scaled by h^-4 = 16 *)\nsc16 = 16; tP1 = {sc16 t7P1[[1, \"tau\"]], sc16 t7P1[[2, \"tau\"]]}; dP1 = {t7P1[[1, \"Delta\"]], t7P1[[2, \"Delta\"]]}; BP1 = (dP1[[1]] - dP1[[2]])/(tP1[[1]] - tP1[[2]]); AP1 = dP1[[1]] - BP1 tP1[[1]];\np1A = <|\"Delta1+Delta2\" -> Total[dP1], \"Delta1 Delta2\" -> dP1[[1]] dP1[[2]], \"tau1+tau2\" -> Total[tP1], \"tau1 tau2\" -> tP1[[1]] tP1[[2]], \"A\" -> AP1, \"B\" -> BP1|>;\nGrid[Join[{{\"series\", \"found (m, n, test res, P, Q)\", \"P1 value\", \"formula at t = 62/35\"}}, Table[{k, ToString[coefTab[fitsA[k]]], N[p1A[k], 9], If[fitsA[k] === None, \"-\", N[fitsA[k][\"ev\"][62/35], 9]]}, {k, Keys[seriesA]}]], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Follow-up result (Tasks 6-7)\n\n**Task 6 verdict: the 62/105 law was a LEAK; the corrected law is K/S = -t/(3(t-2)), kappa_singlet = 1 + K/S = 2(t-3)/(3(t-2)).** Cause: `DownValues` has attribute HoldAll, so the `purge[]` of Task 4 (`Do[DownValues[f] = ..., {f, {Tm, tBasisC, tZof, wgt, branchesAt}}]`) assigned to the iterator f and purged nothing; the memoized transfer matrices (`Tm`, `tBasisC`) of the first point stayed in use while y0, th12 were reset. The scan therefore had P1's transfer matrices and the new resolvent point: K/S = -t12(P1)/(3(t-2)) = -(62/105)/(t-2). Everything at P1 itself (Tasks 1-3, 5 and the P1 part of Task 4) is unaffected. Fixed purge uses literal symbols (cell 36).\n\n(a) Fresh kernels (restart, cell 3 evaluated with the test point in place of the P1 line, cells 4-9, 14, 35), K/S Richardson at om A: (h, theta) = (1, (5/2,0)): -1.6666666666672 vs corrected law -5/3 (diff 5e-13), scan value had been -1.180952381; (1/3, (1/5,-4/9)), t = 29/15: 9.6666666666674 vs law 9.6666666666667 (diff 7e-13), old scan 8.857142857. (b) h = 1, t = 7/3: phi: -2.3333333333339, phi' = (-2/5,3/8,7/11): -2.3333333333343, law -7/3. Corrected 8-point scan (setPoint with fixed purge, both om): max |K/S + t/(3(t-2))| = 3.1e-11 (t = 29/15, 5/2, 3/2, 7/3, 11/4, 13/5, 9/4, 17/6); phi' at 7/3: -2.33333333333427; h = 1/3 via setPoint: 9.66666666666741. Law confirmed leak-free, h- and phi-independent.\n\n**Task 7** (h = 1, theta = (t,0), phi = phiP, om1 = 3/4; slopes from three eps, R_c and tau_c Richardson over three eps; copies sorted by tau; 22 values of t). Delta_c = slope_c + (t-2) R_c. tau_c = eigenvalue of t2 at u = theta1 + h; t2 has degree 4 in (u, theta, h), so tau/h^4 is the h-independent quantity (P1: factor 16; with it P1 agrees with the h = 1 formulas to 8 digits for every series below).\n\nTable (t: Delta1, Delta2, tau1, tau2): 29/15: -1.46172486424, 0.404968107490, 9.76840506217, 24.0582616045; 5/2: -2.50844796455, 0.190266146333, 18.0942434347, 35.9057565653; 3/2: -0.734187472982, 0.567520806319, 4.64231274307, 16.3576872569; 7/3: -2.19105606568, 0.253556065662, 15.4518060262, 32.2148606405; 11/4: -2.99736618199, 0.0951922688592, 22.3631121327, 41.7618878673; 13/5: -2.70225385684, 0.152253856795, 19.7577443106, 38.2022556894; 9/4: -2.03516470509, 0.285164705082, 14.1913470646, 30.4336529354; 17/6: -3.16347254448, 0.0634725443691, 23.8677676193, 43.7988990473 (19/7, 8/3 and the 12 further t are in cells 37 and 39). Symmetric combinations rationalized (1e-9), e.g. t = 29/15: Delta1+Delta2 = -391/370, Delta1 Delta2 = -4928/8325, tau1+tau2 = 2537/75, tau1 tau2 = 1321936/5625; t = 5/2: Delta1+Delta2 = -51/22.\n\nFits (22 points, trained on 15, validated on 7; relative residual on the held-out points):\n- tau1+tau2 = 6t^2 + 9t - 6 = 3(2t-1)(t+2): polynomial (2,0), validation 2.4e-21.\n- tau1 tau2 = 9t^4 + 27t^3 - 9t^2 - 27t = 9t(t-1)(t+1)(t+3): (4,0), 2.1e-22.\n- Delta1 + Delta2 = 3(2-t^2)/(t+3): (2,1), 4.8e-12.\n- Delta1 Delta2 = (t-3)(t-1)(t+1)/(t+3): (3,1), 1.6e-11.\n- Ansatz Delta_c = A(t) + B(t) tau_c holds with A = 1 - t^2 (polynomial (2,0), 2.2e-11) and B = t/(3(t+3)) (rational (1,1), 3.7e-11); consistent: 2A + B(tau1+tau2) = 3(2-t^2)/(t+3) exactly.\n- The cell-38 test restricted to degree <= 2/<= 2 on 7 points: only Delta1+Delta2 fits (1e-13); the tau products and Delta1 Delta2 need the higher degrees above (the P1 mismatch in cell 38 for tau series is only the missing h^4 factor).\n- (i) Delta1 = Delta2 is false (e.g. -2.508 vs 0.190 at t = 5/2).\n\nSo Delta_c = (1 - t^2) + t tau_c/(3(t+3)), with tau_c the two roots of tau^2 - 3(2t-1)(t+2) tau + 9t(t-1)(t+1)(t+3) = 0 (units h = 1; tau/h^4 in general).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## FINAL: pure Q-side end-to-end CG extraction (P1, P2, P3)",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
