  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### FINAL: CG coefficients of adj(x)adj from the det6 x det2 formula\n\n**Formulas.** Overlap identity: <v1(x)v2|Psi_B>/<x0|Psi_B> = c det6[Q_B, Q_vac,(w1,w2)]/Psi_Q^B(x0) x det2^(1)[Q_B; y]/minor1(B), y = w2 y0, y0 = (theta12-h)/(theta12-2h), regime z = 1+eps phi, w1 = 1+eps om1, w2 = 1+eps om2, t = theta12/h. Qnum(B) = R_Q(B)/R_Q(top) <v1(x)v2|e1(x)e1>/<x0|e1(x)e1>. Undone covector phi = delta^Lambda e1^T rho(n'), delta^Lambda = d1^2 d2, d_k = 1/(w2-z_k); at eps = 0: a'0 = (om1-phi1)(phi2-phi1)/((om1-phi2)(om2-phi2)), c'0 = r3(0)(phi3-phi2)/(om2-phi3), r3(0) = (om1-phi2)(phi1-phi3)/((phi1-phi2)(om1-phi3)). CG data (chain side = P_HW Psi slices, <x0|Psi> = 1; Q side from Qnum only):\n- 27: Qnum/delta^Lambda = [Psi_top]_11.\n- [4,1,1]: C = Qnum/(delta^Lambda c'0), [3,3,0]: C = Qnum/(delta^Lambda a'0); limits of C eps^3.\n- octet copy c: (u+u').C_c = Qnum/(delta^Lambda a'0 c'0) (F0 = limit of eps^4 x this, u = e1^T E13, u' = e1^T E23 E12, u+u' = (1,3) on the (1,1,1) indices); mixing R_c = (u.C_c)/((u+u').C_c) = (Delta_c - slope_c)/(t-2), slope_c = om2-slope of F1/F0 for the top-killed Qnum - T (T = delta^Lambda <v2(x)v2|Psi> from det6 with the vacuum Q's of (w1,y)); Delta_c = (1-t^2) + t tau_c/(3(t+3)) (h = 1; tau/h^4 in general), tau_c = t2(theta1+h) = chi3 nu1(theta1+h) nu2(theta1) Q^j(theta1-h)/Q^j(theta1) (j-independent), the two roots of tau^2 - 3(2t-1)(t+2) tau + 9t(t-1)(t+1)(t+3) = 0.\n- singlet: C = Qnum/(kappa phi012), phi012 = exact (0,1,2) component of the covector, kappa = 1 + K/S = 2(t-3)/(3(t-2)), limit of C eps^6.\nPrecision: Q numbers keep 126 digits at pr = 200; all limits Richardson (eps = 1e-6, 2e-6, 4e-6).\n\n**P1 (h = 1/2, theta = (2/7,-3/5), t = 62/35).** [error at eps = 1e-6, max over the 18 om | Q limit | chain limit | agreement]: 27: 0 | 2.609467456 | 2.609467456 | 0; [4,1,1]: 7.89e-7 | 46.67453891 | 46.67453891 | 1.2e-19; [3,3,0]: 9.35e-7 | 10.92853892 | 10.92853892 | 1.6e-121; octet 1 functional: 3.40e-6 | 184.3305612 | 184.3305612 | 3.2e-20; octet 2: 1.82e-6 | -238.5587523 | -238.5587523 | 9.5e-20; singlet: 1.47e-6 | -5118.538314 | -5118.538314 | 4.5e-19. Octet mixing: copy 1: slope_Q -1.56871932, tau_Q = tau_eig = 7.72932830 (j-spread 0), Delta = -1.18143552, R^Q = -1.69436661, R^chain = -1.69436661 (|diff| 4.9e-11); copy 2: slope 0.716366881, tau 21.0412839, Delta 0.465952203, R^Q = R^chain = 1.09556421 (3.7e-11).\n\n**P2 (h = 1/3, theta = (1/5,-4/9), t = 29/15, y0 = -14; t in the Delta fit set).** 27: 0 | 2.609467456 | 2.609467456 | 0; [4,1,1]: 1.11e-6 | 38.57793522 | 38.57793522 | 6.0e-20; [3,3,0]: 1.13e-6 | 9.032771962 | 9.032771962 | 9.7e-121; octet 1: 3.61e-6 | 122.3424387 | 122.3424387 | 2.8e-20; octet 2: 1.18e-6 | -245.4884068 | -245.4884068 | 1.6e-20; singlet: 1.96e-6 | -3805.202777 | -3805.202777 | 6.4e-19. Octets: copy 1: slope -1.58305272, tau (Q = eig) 9.76840506, Delta -1.46172486, R^Q = R^chain = -1.81991789 (8.4e-11); copy 2: slope 0.476746417, tau 24.0582616, Delta 0.404968107, R = 1.07667465 (5.6e-11).\n\n**P3 (h = 1/2, theta = (3/7,-1/4), t = 19/14, y0 = -5/9; not in any fit set; no om component equals a phi component).** 27: 0 | 2.609467456 | 2.609467456 | 0; [4,1,1]: 7.58e-7 | 100.8170040 | 100.8170040 | 1.8e-19; [3,3,0]: 4.33e-7 | 23.60564406 | 23.60564406 | 3.5e-121; octet 1: 3.05e-6 | 937.1257171 | 937.1257171 | 3.8e-19; octet 2: 3.55e-6 | -254.7138085 | -254.7138085 | 2.9e-19; singlet: 1.09e-6 | -20997.70633 | -20997.70633 | 2.2e-19. Octets: copy 1: slope -1.37387704, tau 3.18098696, Delta -0.511570329, R^Q = R^chain = -1.34136599 (1.2e-11); copy 2: slope 1.36685128, tau 14.0843192, Delta 0.620469626, R = 1.16103812 (5.3e-12).\n\nThe chain eps-exponents of the slices are -2, -3, -3, -4, -4, -6 at all three points. tau_Q from the dual-Q dictionary equals the eigenvalue-based tau (relative difference 0, j-spread 0) at all points. The closed forms kappa(t) and Delta_c(t, tau_c) therefore hold at P1, P2 and the out-of-sample P3 to the 1e-11 level of the Richardson extrapolation.",
